  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At the foot of the village of Le Rayol, this white-sand cove is made up of two beaches, separated by a rocky point from which a staircase serves the east beach. Crystal-clear water, the Îles d'Or in the background, picnic tables overlooking the bay (tourist office). The Domaine du Rayol, the Mediterranean gardens, is very close but does not own the beach.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>From 1 June to 30 September, dogs on a leash are only allowed between 7pm and 8am; outside those hours, they are not allowed. This is the town hall's rule (news item of 23 June 2026 and the summer 2026 "Carnets du Rayol-Canadel-Pramousquier" bulletin), relayed by the Gulf of Saint-Tropez tourist office, and the same as on the neighbouring beaches of <a href="/en/fiche-canadel">Canadel</a> and <a href="/en/fiche-plage-pramousquier-rayol-canadel">Pramousquier</a> (Rayol-Canadel side). Owners must pick up waste. For the rest of the year, neither the town nor the tourist office publishes a precise rule: ask the town hall (04 94 15 61 00).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: in high summer, come early in the morning or in the evening (7pm-8am). The town has removed the bins from the beaches: bring bags for waste.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Domaine du Rayol does not admit pets, even on a leash or in a backpack (Domaine's rules) — plan accordingly if you intend to combine both visits. <a href="/en/fiche-canadel">Canadel beach</a> is nearby, and <a href="/en/fiche-plage-pramousquier-rayol-canadel">Pramousquier beach</a> is 2 km away along the Voie Verte.</p>
    </div>

